From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sat, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: run ahb shutdown() teardown only on WCN6750

The AHB shutdown() callback was introduced solely for WCN6750, which must
stop DMA before its SMMU is torn down. It was registered unconditionally
in ath11k_ahb_driver, so it also runs on the IPQ AHB targets
(IPQ8074/IPQ6018/IPQ5018), which never had a shutdown() handler before and
have no such requirement. On those targets the teardown stops the WCSS Q6
firmware during system reboot/shutdown, leaving shared WCSS state such that
the boot ROM (SBL1) hangs during DDR training on the following warm reset;
only a cold power-on reset recovers.

On the Xiaomi AX3000E (IPQ5018 + QCN6122) this manifests as reboots that do
not come back reliably. Skip the teardown on the non-WCN6750 AHB targets so
a normal reboot lets the SoC reset re-initialize the WCSS from scratch.

This mirrors the upstream fix (ath-next, 2026); the pre-6.18.39 backports
snapshot in this tree still runs the teardown unconditionally.

Fixes: ac41c2b642b1 ("wifi: ath11k: Register shutdown handler for WCN6750")
Signed-off-by: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -1291,6 +1291,18 @@
 	 * remove() is invoked during rmmod & shutdown() during
 	 * system reboot/shutdown.
 	 */
+
+	/* The shutdown() callback was added for WCN6750, which has to stop DMA
+	 * before the SMMU is torn down. The other AHB targets (IPQ8074/IPQ6018/
+	 * IPQ5018) have no such requirement, and running the teardown here stops
+	 * the WCSS Q6 firmware, which leaves shared state that hangs the boot ROM
+	 * (SBL1) during DDR training on the following warm reset -- only a cold
+	 * (power-on) reset recovers. Skip it on those targets; the SoC reset
+	 * re-initializes the WCSS from scratch.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev != ATH11K_HW_WCN6750_HW10)
+		return;
+
 	ath11k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
 
 	if (!(test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags)))
